    "evidence_text": "To analyze pretrained language model performance on QA, we extend the LAMA (Petroni et al., 2019) evaluation framework by a component that is focused on negation.\n\nTo this end, we introduce the negated LAMA dataset.\n\nIn our experiments, we query the pretrained language models with both original LAMA and negated LAMA statements and compare their predictions in terms of rank correlation and overlap of top predictions.\n\nResults\tTable TABREF1 compares the predictions of original LAMA and negated LAMA.\n\nA key problem is that the LAMA setup does not\n\nmore often to a person being born in a city and not born in a country, giving you in both cases more precise information.\n\nIn a case study, they test for correct licensing environments for negative polarity items.\n\nWe take a different approach by focusing on factual knowledge stored in negated statements.\n\ninvestigate the understanding of function words \u2013 among them negation particles \u2013 using an entailment- and classification-based approach.\n\nA supplementary dataset of 16 sentences queries again for the \"to be\" relation only but including more natural sentence structure.\n\nOutput predictions for the original LAMA query and the negated statement are highly correlated.",
